{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01NQtUFtnRiLkXtiRLasnXPC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (one folder, no syncing, plain-markdown source of truth).\n\n- **Purpose** â€” A personal task/project manager that keeps tasks, projects, an inbox, and per-domain work (academic, commercial, family, writing) in plain markdown files, surfaced through a daily dashboard with calendar, focus items, and deadlines.\n\n- **What it ships** â€” Its one declared deliverable is **`anchor_gui.py`**: a stdlib-only Python HTTP server that renders the full dashboard HTML on every request and writes changes straight back to the markdown files. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777` (host `PUTER`/`gwl-server`). A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) provides the same task operations and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Task lifecycle** â€” Tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, each archived to its own markdown file, with optional notes for context.\n\n- **Self-testing** â€” A daily 5 AM health check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) parses every file, boots a throwaway server, exercises all endpoints and state transitions (fully stubbed, never touching live data), and writes a dated report; failures show a red dashboard banner.\n\n- **The R&D control surface (the bulk of recent engineering)** â€” Beyond plain task tracking, Anchor has grown a per-project \"cockpit\" for trio-driven R&D (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). Built across four versions, now at **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (merged to master 2026-06-13, 637 tests green): each project window shows Research/Planning/Build/Deliverables/Grass lanes as **status-light tiles** that expand inline panels combining a cached, grounded summary with a **real, resizable ConPTY terminal** (xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket). Sessions get git-worktree isolation, the lane's skill auto-loads once and greets once, engines toggle between Claude/Gemini, and deliverables launch by type.\n\n- **Constraint that shapes everything** â€” Python stdlib only, with exactly **one** declared native exception: `pywinpty` (lazy import in `pty_manager.py` only) for the optional terminal subsystem, which degrades gracefully if absent. A distribution import-scanner enforces this rule.\n\n- **Branding** â€” Presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢,\" using a single vendored brand mark as favicon and masthead lockup."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c137b643-a87f-405f-b369-259a416322ed","uuid":"1d4d2526-8a90-47a7-87d0-9759e5afa786","request_id":"req_011Cc1JRq4bNuNXRQNQV2wuA"}
